# Frontend Engineering Rules (SmartAttend UI)

1. **Modular Architecture:**
   - Organize JavaScript into modular namespaces/IIFEs to avoid global pollution.
   - All network calls must pass through `ApiClient` in `src/main/resources/static/js/api.js`.
2. **Design Tokens & Theme Consistency:**
   - Adhere strictly to the color palette in `docs/DESIGN.md`:
     - Safe ($>85\%$): Emerald `#10B981`
     - Warning ($75\%\text{--}84\%$): Amber `#F59E0B`
     - Shortage ($<75\%$): Crimson `#EF4444`
     - Condonation ($60\%\text{--}74.99\%$): Rose `#F43F5E`
3. **Real-Time SSE Event Handling:**
   - Always verify and close native `EventSource` connections on page unload.
   - Smoothly animate UI counter updates with CSS pulses instead of abrupt re-renders.
4. **XSS Protection:**
   - Render untrusted user inputs (student names, roll numbers, remarks) using `.textContent` or safe DOM text creation.
